{"candidate_id": "c001", "parent": null, "source_sha256": "5e94b0ce7a6b56c81c5af357a9f9b38d07cb8c92a93d7393fcce70156e478cff", "hypothesis": "Correctness anchor: 3-kernel Triton decomposition (K1 GEMM1+bias, K2 fused gating+causal depthwise conv+gating, K3 GEMM2+bias) entirely in (M,H) row-major space, eliminating the reference's two transposes and .contiguous() copy; fp32 middle; single conservative tile (64x64x32, warps=4, stages=3). Goal: pass all 5 workloads and read the Triton-vs-cuBLAS GEMM gap.", "change_vs_parent": "initial baseline", "validation": {"analytical_checks": ["chunk offsets Bgate[0,H)/Cgate[H,2H)/Xproj[2H,3H)", "conv cross-correlation tap: k=3=current, d=(KC-1)-k", "causal+batch-boundary mask s>=d", "F.linear W^T", "fp32 GEMM+conv accum, bf16 store"], "expected_correct": true}, "results": {"b0a9e3f0": {"axes": {"B": 1, "S": 1024}, "correct": true, "speedup": 1.1672}, "8b678b13": {"axes": {"B": 4, "S": 256}, "correct": true, "speedup": 1.1714}, "58e3ac47": {"axes": {"B": 32, "S": 256}, "correct": true, "speedup": 0.8887}, "6033fd0f": {"axes": {"B": 2, "S": 4096}, "correct": true, "speedup": 1.0255}, "bb262a64": {"axes": {"B": 1, "S": 2048}, "correct": true, "speedup": 1.1842}}, "geomean_speedup": 1.0809, "all_correct": true, "decision": "accept", "decision_reason": "All 5 workloads correct; baseline geomean 1.0809x. WL3 (M=8192, B=32,S=256) at 0.8887x is the weak point: conservative 64x64x32 tile underperforms cuBLAS at large M, confirming prediction P1 (GEMM tuning highest leverage). Set as current best-correct.", "cumulative_evals": 1, "skill_usage": "none (KernelWiki N/A for sm_80; profiler disallowed)"}
{"candidate_id": "c002", "parent": "c001", "source_sha256": "e3125cb9dd66a438a90eac8a6e9f008c2defec7da35c9689fa2815d304eef8b2", "hypothesis": "Phase B (P1): c001's fixed 64x64x32 GEMM tile underperforms cuBLAS at large M (WL3 0.889x). Add @triton.autotune over a curated Ampere bf16 tile menu on the shared GEMM kernel (used by both K1 and K3), keyed on (M,N,K). All feedback shapes are mask-free (M mult 256, N mult 256, K mult 128). Expect the single largest geomean jump, especially recovering WL3 to >=1x.", "change_vs_parent": "Added @triton.autotune (11 configs: BLOCK_M/N in {64,128,256}, BLOCK_K in {32,64}, GROUP_M=8, stages 3-4, warps 4-8) on _gemm_bias_kernel keyed on (M,N,K); removed fixed per-call BLOCK/warps/stages; grid lambdas now read META['BLOCK_M/N']. K2 fused conv kernel and all numerics unchanged.", "validation": {"analytical_checks": ["kernel math identical to c001 (only tile-selection policy changed)", "all feedback shapes divide every tile evenly -> mask-free correctness preserved", "fp32 accum + bf16 store unchanged", "K2 unchanged"], "expected_correct": true}, "results": {"b0a9e3f0": {"axes": {"B": 1, "S": 1024}, "correct": true, "speedup": 1.6626}, "8b678b13": {"axes": {"B": 4, "S": 256}, "correct": true, "speedup": 1.6746}, "58e3ac47": {"axes": {"B": 32, "S": 256}, "correct": true, "speedup": 1.3147}, "6033fd0f": {"axes": {"B": 2, "S": 4096}, "correct": true, "speedup": 1.3296}, "bb262a64": {"axes": {"B": 1, "S": 2048}, "correct": true, "speedup": 1.4000}}, "geomean_speedup": 1.4678, "all_correct": true, "decision": "accept", "decision_reason": "All 5 correct; geomean 1.0809x -> 1.4678x (+35.8%), the single largest jump so far, confirming prediction P1 (GEMMs dominate, tile policy is the primary lever). WL3 recovered from 0.889x to 1.315x. New current best-correct. Next: Phase C (fuse/tile the memory-bound K2) since GEMM tuning is largely captured; small-M cases (WL1/2 at ~1.66x) now lead, large-M (WL3/4 ~1.32x) lag -> remaining headroom is intermediate-traffic + launch overhead reduction.", "cumulative_evals": 2, "skill_usage": "none (KernelWiki N/A for sm_80; profiler disallowed)"}
{"candidate_id": "c003", "parent": "c002", "source_sha256": "b19cb64757825d4656a1eeb992bac072abcd38e7f2eaac46adff124f835bab3b", "hypothesis": "Phase C (P2): K2 (fused gating+causal-conv+gating) is memory-bound and was left at a fixed conservative 64x64/warps=4 tile in c001/c002. Add @triton.autotune over a K2 launch-config menu (BLOCK_M in {16,32,64,128}, BLOCK_H in {64,128,256}, num_warps {4,8}) keyed on (M,S,H), favoring large coalesced BLOCK_H along the contiguous H axis. Kernel math byte-for-byte identical to c002 (only launch policy tuned); baseline 64x64/w4 retained so autotune picks min over a superset. Expect a small gain (draft P2: middle is minor vs GEMMs), most visible on large-M WL3/WL4 where K2 traffic is largest.", "change_vs_parent": "Added @triton.autotune (9 configs) on _fused_conv_kernel keyed on (M,S,H); removed fixed _BM2/_BH2=64 launch; grid2 now reads META['BLOCK_M','BLOCK_H']. GEMM kernel, its autotune menu, and all numerics unchanged.", "validation": {"analytical_checks": ["K2 math identical to c002 (only tile-selection policy changed)", "per-row guard s=offs_m%S; valid=s>=d handles causal pad + batch boundary for ANY (BLOCK_M,BLOCK_H) incl. tiles spanning batches", "every tensor dim masked (m_mask,h_mask) -> M/H overhang safe", "acc regs/thread = BLOCK_M*BLOCK_H/(32*num_warps) <= 64 -> no spills", "GEMM path unchanged -> GEMM correctness preserved"], "expected_correct": true}, "results": {"b0a9e3f0": {"axes": {"B": 1, "S": 1024}, "correct": true, "speedup": 1.6554}, "8b678b13": {"axes": {"B": 4, "S": 256}, "correct": true, "speedup": 1.6681}, "58e3ac47": {"axes": {"B": 32, "S": 256}, "correct": true, "speedup": 1.3336}, "6033fd0f": {"axes": {"B": 2, "S": 4096}, "correct": true, "speedup": 1.3419}, "bb262a64": {"axes": {"B": 1, "S": 2048}, "correct": true, "speedup": 1.4007}}, "geomean_speedup": 1.4724, "all_correct": true, "decision": "accept", "decision_reason": "All 5 correct; geomean 1.4678x -> 1.4724x (+0.31%). Confirms prediction P2: the memory-bound middle is minor vs the GEMMs, so tuning K2 yields only a small gain. Gain concentrated on large-M cases WL3 (1.3147->1.3336) and WL4 (1.3296->1.3419) where K2 traffic is largest, as predicted; small-M WL1/WL2 dipped ~0.4-0.6% (autotune timing noise, within measurement variance) and WL5 flat. New current best-correct (1.4724x >= 1.4678x). Remaining headroom is now almost entirely in the GEMMs (which dominate) and in eliminating the intermediate BCx(M,3H)/y(M,H) write+read via fusion (F1: fold input gating into GEMM1 epilogue).", "cumulative_evals": 3, "skill_usage": "none (KernelWiki N/A for sm_80; profiler disallowed)"}
